{
  "dom_id": "step-q264821",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z,w)=zw{e}^{xy}$, compute ${∇}_{x,z}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">${∇}_{x,z}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "To compute ${∇}_{x,z}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $z$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(zw{e}^{xy}) & =yzw{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{∂}{∂z}(zw{e}^{xy}) & =w{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,z}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}yzw{e}^{xy} \\\\ w{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
